        "original_id": "d9b4ca40-c62d-54e4-93e0-ac1d42999e91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luis Gianneo, Ariel Ramírez, Marta Lambertini, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, Rodolfo Arizaga, Roberto Caamaño, Gerardo Gandini\n- Roles: music educator, composer, pianist, music director, student\n- Places: San Isidro, Buenos Aires, Universidad Católica Argentina\n\nFacts:\n- Ariel Ramírez was born on 4 September 1921 and died on 18 February 2010.\n- Ariel Ramírez was an Argentine composer, pianist, and music director.\n- Luis Gianneo worked as a music educator and taught composers Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, and Rodolfo Arizaga.\n- Marta Lambertini was born in San Isidro, Buenos Aires.\n- Marta Lambertini studied at the Universidad Católica Argentina with Roberto Caamaño, Luis Gianneo, and Gerardo Gandini, and she graduated in 1972.",
